    "bio": "a Representative from Virginia; born in Richmond, Va., August 31, 1930; attended public schools; B.S., Virginia Polytechnic Institute, Blacksburg, 1952; LL.B., University of Richmond Law School, 1955; admitted to the Virginia State bar in 1955 and commenced practice in Richmond; member, Virginia house of delegates, 1972-1986; elected as a Democrat to the One Hundredth and six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1987-January 3, 2001); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Seventh Congress; died on October 27, 2010, in Virginia Beach, Va.; interment at Taylorsville Baptist Church Cemetery, Taylorsville, Va.",
